        "original_id": "fe73c256-6515-530b-87d4-a63432cc455a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Badham, Michael J. Fox, James Woods, Mos Def, Yasiin Bey, Arthur B. Rubinstein\n- Works: The Hard Way, Black on Both Sides\n- Groups and Labels: Urban Thermo Dynamics, Da Bush Babees, De La Soul, Rawkus Records\n- Topics: film cast, hip hop career, film music credits\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur B. Rubinstein worked on films including \"The Hard Way\" in 1991, alongside other credits from 1981 to 1995.\n- \"The Hard Way\" is a 1991 American action comedy film directed by John Badham and starring Michael J. Fox and James Woods.\n- \"The Hard Way\" features supporting roles by Stephen Lang, Annabella Sciorra, Luis Guzmán, LL Cool J, Delroy Lindo, Christina Ricci, Mos Def, Kathy Najimy, Michael Badalucco, and Lewis Black.\n- Yasiin Bey, born Dante Terrell Smith on December 11, 1973, is an American hip hop recording artist, actor, and activist from Brooklyn, New York City, best known by the stage name Mos Def.\n- Mos Def began his hip hop career in 1994 with his siblings in the short-lived rap group Urban Thermo Dynamics.\n- After Urban Thermo Dynamics, Mos Def appeared on albums by Da Bush Babees and De La Soul.\n- Mos Def was on the roster of Rawkus Records and released his 1999 solo debut album, \"Black on Both Sides\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
